{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: duplicate routing — `_tuiPickAddProvider` could stay the single router**

The pick is dispatched with a re-implemented copy of `_tuiPickAddProvider`'s routing:

```dart
} else if (choice == 'custom') {
  await _startProviderFlow();
} else {
  await _addProviderHandlers[choice]?.call();
}
```

The doc comment says the choice "routes … like `[_tuiPickAddProvider]`", but the link is by convention only — if the TUI router changes (e.g. `custom` gains a pre-step, or a preset key is remapped), boarding drifts silently.

It can be reused directly: keep the raw `preset:` prefix in the option keys and hand the answer to the existing router (which already strips the prefix and owns the `custom` branch):

```dart
final choice = await _pickOption('choose provider', [
  for (final item in _addProviderItems()) (item.key, item.label, item.description),
]);
// Release the flow gate so the sub-flow can take its own lock.
_providerFlowActive = false;
if (choice == null) {
  io.writeln('provider setup cancelled');
} else {
  await _tuiPickAddProvider(choice);
}
```

(Only reason to keep the current shape: stripped keys read slightly better in future logs. Not blocking either way.)
